{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":24133,"duration_api_ms":25392,"num_turns":8,"result":"I wrote `src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run it. This environment didn't let me check for bpftrace or root access.\n\nRun it with `sudo bpftrace src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`.\n\nIt hooks the `power:cpu_frequency` tracepoint. While it runs, it prints each frequency change as time, CPU, old MHz and new MHz. On Ctrl-C it prints three summaries:\n- the number of changes per CPU\n- the milliseconds each CPU spent at each frequency\n- a histogram of the frequencies seen\n\nThe tracepoint only fires when the kernel reports a frequency change. VMs, and some drivers such as `intel_pstate` in active mode, may show little or nothing. In that case, try `cpupower frequency-set -g powersave` or `-g performance`, or run a CPU-heavy load to trigger changes.\n\nI can add a README and Makefile to match the other tutorials if you want them.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dc35a605-192f-4a15-b53d-7a8d740a8744","total_cost_usd":0.09010884999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2815,"cache_read_input_tokens":155932,"output_tokens":2152,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2815},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":327,"cache_read_input_tokens":27391,"cache_creation_input_tokens":702,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":702,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":2152,"cacheReadInputTokens":155932,"cacheCreationInputTokens":2815,"webSea